Product Requirements Document (PRD)
Project Title: 30done
Owner: Juan Allo Ron
Version: 1.0
Date: June 19, 2025

1. Objective
Build a mobile/web app that helps users commit to and complete 30-day fitness challenges like the “Cardio 30-Day Challenge.” The app enables users to select a challenge, receive daily reminders, view exercise instructions, and track progress with a visual “don’t break the chain” system.

2. Target Users
Fitness enthusiasts following challenge calendars from sources like Neila Rey, Chloe Ting, etc.

Beginners wanting simple, guided routines.

Busy professionals looking for short, structured exercise routines.

Habit-builders using streak-based motivation.

3. Key Features
3.1 Challenge Library
List of available challenges (e.g., Cardio 30-Day Challenge).

Each challenge includes:

Title and duration

Daily breakdown

Exercise illustrations/screenshots

Estimated time per day

3.2 Daily Tracker
“Don’t break the chain” calendar view

Mark day as “Completed” or “Skipped”

Auto-progress to next day after completion

History view for past days

3.3 Exercise View
Daily view with:

Today’s workout details (e.g., “100 high knees, 40 climbers”)

Visual instructions (images or GIFs)

Optional timer

3.4 Notifications / Reminders
Daily reminders at user-selected time

Smart nudges if workout hasn’t been logged by evening

3.5 Progress & Streaks
Streak counter

Completion percentage

Ability to restart/reset challenge

4. Optional (Nice to Have)
Audio/voice instructions

Custom challenge creation

Social sharing or community challenges

Apple Health / Google Fit integration

In-app challenges with increasing difficulty

5. UX Notes
Minimal, clear UI — no account needed to get started

Emphasis on visual progress (checkmarks, streak chain)

Fast onboarding: “Pick a challenge → Set reminder → Start today”

6. Technical Requirements
Platform
MVP: Mobile-first PWA or Native (Flutter or React Native)

Optionally expand to web dashboard

Data Storage
Local DB for offline use (e.g., SQLite)

Optional cloud sync with login (Firebase or Supabase)

Stack Suggestions
React Native or Flutter

Firebase Auth (optional), Firestore/SQLite for data

Push Notifications via OneSignal / Firebase Messaging

7. User Stories
User Story 1: Select a Challenge
As a user, I want to browse a list of challenges so I can pick one that fits my goals.

User Story 2: See Today’s Task
As a user, I want to view today’s workout so I know what exercises to do.

User Story 3: Complete a Day
As a user, I want to check off a day so I can track my progress.

User Story 4: View Progress
As a user, I want to see my streak and history so I stay motivated.

User Story 5: Get Reminders
As a user, I want daily notifications so I don’t forget to work out.

8. Success Metrics
Daily active users (DAU)

Average streak length per user

Challenge completion rate

User retention at day 7, 14, 30

9. Future Ideas
AI-generated custom challenges

Challenge marketplace

Friend challenges / group tracking

Streak repair with tokens (gamified model)